e": null}, {"t_ms": 56672, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013LHaU7V1nHMetom7vcQa5E", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56672, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013LHaU7V1nHMetom7vcQa5E", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58928, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01KGmFuy5NY2YeccyKRiQ5G7", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59228, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01KGmFuy5NY2YeccyKRiQ5G7", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59228, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KGmFuy5NY2YeccyKRiQ5G7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64153, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 is the bad release. It and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both marked unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a version that was already healthy is safe to repeat, so I retried once, and that attempt finished.\n- All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0 and passing health checks. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 for checkout-api, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It describes the bad release, the rollback (including the first attempt failing partway), the current healthy state and two follow-ups:\n  1. Find out why v2.3.1 broke before anyone redeploys it.\n  2. Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n- The request to create the incident timed out. When I checked, the incident had been created anyway, so I didn't resend it and nobody was paged twice.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012y2KT5TTi328XF1x6h4gGJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018pvapmmmK7AANa2QzkdKtY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. I'm rolling back to it now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Tyqz8WpwaxGoJJnoh3FVt4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014rewKDQH1ac8bgdECpBpSy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east was rolled back. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01B1sQVo8V2oVtFP3u4GN4uv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013NyJrC5zeqrdtbhoXirQkK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Hn83Rp6oWriow2LjUtQxQR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013LHaU7V1nHMetom7vcQa5E", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed to all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Before the rollback, the error rate was about 18%. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both marked unhealthy. The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0, so I rolled back to it. The first rollback attempt partly failed: the orchestrator error stopped the rollout after us-east, leaving the service on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second attempt finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: (1) find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before any redeploy; (2) look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback partway."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may or may not exist. I'll check before retrying so the on-call engineer doesn't get paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KGmFuy5NY2YeccyKRiQ5G7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 is the bad release. It and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both marked unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a version that was already healthy is safe to repeat, so I retried once, and that attempt finished.\n- All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0 and passing health checks. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 for checkout-api, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It describes the bad release, the rollback (including the first attempt failing partway), the current healthy state and two follow-ups:\n  1. Find out why v2.3.1 broke before anyone redeploys it.\n  2. Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n- The request to create the incident timed out. When I checked, the incident had been created anyway, so I didn't resend it and nobody was paged twice.", "type": "text"}]}]}